            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0742" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.001W64/93: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-13T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3724. Your 7047, December 7, 1 p.m.</p>
                <p>Department is without information in this matter. For your information and
                    guidance following are quotations from telegram to Ammission, Paris, November
                        27:<anchor n="9" xml:id="d618-f1"/> “In view of the failure of the Senate to
                    ratify the treaty the President feels that you should withdraw immediately the
                    American representatives on all commissions growing out of or dependent on
                    either the Peace Conference or the treaty” and “Until the Senate takes some
                    action the Department proposes to express no opinion concerning questions
                    arising under the terms of the treaty except those in which it may interest
                    itself because of the necessity to protect American interests.”</p>
                <p>Following out policy above indicated the United States will not at present
                    support any demand for the extradition of the ex-Kaiser or participate in any
                    way in his trial should it occur.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
